{
  "class": "ClientChatMessagePacket",
  "module": "client/play/client_chat_message_packet",
  "module_docs": [
    "Port of `net.minestom.server.network.packet.client.play.ClientChatMessagePacket`.",
    "",
    "# Local representations",
    "",
    "- `signature` is the ported `crypto::MessageSignature` \u2014 Java's",
    "  `MessageSignature` is exactly 256 bytes, which the ported type enforces.",
    "- `ack_list` is Java's `FixedBitSet(20)`. A `BitSet` has no Rust equivalent,",
    "  so the 20 bits are held as the little-endian bit-index mask Java's",
    "  `BitSet.toByteArray`/`BitSet.valueOf` exchange; [`ACK_LIST_BYTES`] is the",
    "  `(20 + 7) / Long.BYTES` byte length the wire type writes."
  ],
